        <h1>LeetCode 3903: Smallest Stable Index I (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given an integer array nums of length n and an integer k. For every index i, its
                instability score is defined as the maximum value among nums[0..i] minus the minimum value
                among nums[i..n-1]. An index i is considered stable if its instability score is less than or
                equal to k. Return the smallest stable index, or -1 if no such index exists.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: nums = [5,0,1,4], k = 3<br>
                Output: 3<br>
                Explanation: At index 3, the maximum of [5,0,1,4] is 5 and the minimum of [4] is 4, giving an
                instability score of 1, which is the first score at or below k = 3.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    static int firstStableIndex(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; nums, int k) {
        const int size = nums.size();
        int suffixMin[size], minimum = nums.back();
        for (int index = size - 1; index &gt;= 0; index--) {
            minimum = min(nums[index], minimum);
            suffixMin[index] = minimum;
        }
        int maximum = -1;
        for (int index = 0; index &lt; size; index++) {
            maximum = max(maximum, nums[index]);
            if (maximum - suffixMin[index] &lt;= k) return index;
        }
        return -1;
    }
};</code></pre>
